WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.935 --> 00:00:18.415
Noah's grandma was moving into an apartment.

2
00:00:18.416 --> 00:00:23.452
He and his parents were going to her house to help her clean up and pack.

3
00:00:23.453 --> 00:00:30.351
"I hope this doesn't take all day," Noah thought on the drive over.

4
00:00:30.352 --> 00:00:36.311
"I have lots of stuff," Grandma said when they arrived.

5
00:00:36.312 --> 00:00:41.812
"I have some things that you'll be very excited about, Noah."

6
00:00:41.813 --> 00:00:44.937
Noah smiled politely.

7
00:00:44.938 --> 00:00:48.781
Grandma really did have lots of stuff.

8
00:00:48.782 --> 00:00:53.285
But it was mostly dishes, vases, and old pictures.

9
00:00:53.286 --> 00:00:56.236
None of that was exciting.

10
00:00:56.237 --> 00:01:00.218
Mom and Dad started sorting items in the living room.

11
00:01:00.219 --> 00:01:04.440
Grandma was going to take some of those things to her new apartment.

12
00:01:04.441 --> 00:01:07.541
She was going to donate the rest of them.

13
00:01:07.542 --> 00:01:11.123
"Come with me, Noah," Grandma said.

14
00:01:11.124 --> 00:01:18.259
"I have something to show you."

15
00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:20.827
They went into a small room.

16
00:01:20.828 --> 00:01:26.868
Noah saw lots of long, white boxes.

17
00:01:26.869 --> 00:01:30.680
"What's in those boxes?" he asked.

18
00:01:30.681 --> 00:01:37.632
"See for yourself," Grandma said.

19
00:01:37.633 --> 00:01:40.849
Noah opened a box.

20
00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:43.958
It was filled with comic books.

21
00:01:43.959 --> 00:01:46.211
Each was wrapped in plastic.

22
00:01:46.212 --> 00:01:49.663
"I didn't know you liked comic books, Grandma!"

23
00:01:49.664 --> 00:01:52.242
Grandma chuckled.

24
00:01:52.243 --> 00:01:56.476
"I've been collecting them since I was a little girl.

25
00:01:56.477 --> 00:02:02.175
Some are pretty old. Most are in mint condition though."

26
00:02:02.176 --> 00:02:05.862
"What does that mean?" Noah asked.

27
00:02:05.863 --> 00:02:10.651
"Comic books are graded on their condition," Grandma said.

28
00:02:10.652 --> 00:02:16.212
"If a comic book is torn or damaged, it's in poor condition.

29
00:02:16.213 --> 00:02:24.407
When a comic book still looks brand-new, it's in mint condition."

30
00:02:24.408 --> 00:02:30.215
"If a comic book is in mint condition, is it worth a lot of money?" Noah asked.

31
00:02:30.216 --> 00:02:33.948
"Sometimes," Grandma said.

32
00:02:33.949 --> 00:02:38.678
"A comic book's value depends on different things.

33
00:02:38.679 --> 00:02:41.652
Some comic books are rare.

34
00:02:41.653 --> 00:02:45.891
Some contain the first appearance of a superhero.

35
00:02:45.892 --> 00:02:49.414
Others were illustrated by a famous artist.

36
00:02:49.415 --> 00:02:53.896
Those comic books can be very valuable.

37
00:02:53.897 --> 00:03:00.816
Of course, a comic book is only worth the price someone is willing to pay for it."

38
00:03:00.817 --> 00:03:06.141
Grandma took out a small box and unlocked it.

39
00:03:06.142 --> 00:03:10.681
"These are my most valuable comic books.

40
00:03:10.682 --> 00:03:15.042
This one is the first issue of Super Comics.

41
00:03:15.043 --> 00:03:21.696
And this one is the first issue where the Human Spider had his black costume.

42
00:03:21.697 --> 00:03:27.227
Before that he always wore a purple costume."

43
00:03:27.228 --> 00:03:32.596
"Wow!" Noah said. "I love the Human Spider!"

44
00:03:32.597 --> 00:03:39.659
Grandma smiled. "I'm going to give most of my collection to you."

45
00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:44.683
Noah was shocked. "Really?"

46
00:03:44.684 --> 00:03:46.500
Grandma nodded.

47
00:03:46.501 --> 00:03:52.441
She locked the small box and rested her hand on it. "But not these."

48
00:03:52.442 --> 00:03:55.643
"Oh, okay," Noah murmured.

49
00:03:55.644 --> 00:03:58.535
He felt a little disappointed.

50
00:03:58.536 --> 00:04:02.443
Why couldn't he have those comic books?

51
00:04:02.444 --> 00:04:06.554
Grandma must have known what he was thinking.

52
00:04:06.555 --> 00:04:11.204
"The comic books in this box are worth a fortune, Noah.

53
00:04:11.205 --> 00:04:13.498
I'm going to sell them.

54
00:04:13.499 --> 00:04:18.074
The money will help pay for your college education."

55
00:04:18.075 --> 00:04:21.380
"I might not be able to go to college, Grandma."

56
00:04:21.381 --> 00:04:26.119
Grandma raised an eyebrow. "What do you mean?"

57
00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:32.967
Noah grinned. "I'll be too busy reading the rest of your comic books!"

58
00:04:32.968 --> 00:04:41.443
Grandma laughed. "Very funny, Noah!"
